{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2170-06-03 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Ms. ___ . I'm Dr. ___ , part of the surgery team. You're here for cardiac optimization before your planned left below-the-knee amputation, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2170-06-03 11:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. My foot ulcer hasn’t healed, and they said it’s time. I’m nervous about the surgery and my heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2170-06-03 11:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely understandable. We’re going to make sure your heart is stable before the surgery. We’ll do a stress test and work closely with cardiology."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2170-06-03 11:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had heart issues before—CHF, AFib, and a bypass. Will that make the surgery riskier?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2170-06-03 11:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, those do increase risk, which is why we’re taking this step of cardiac optimization. We want to reduce any complications during or after surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2170-06-03 11:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. What tests will I have?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2170-06-03 11:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll have a P-MIBI stress test to check for heart ischemia. We’ll also do a chest X-ray today to check your lungs and heart size."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2170-06-03 11:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my dialysis? I’m on it three times a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2170-06-03 11:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll continue your regular hemodialysis schedule. We’ve scheduled sessions before surgery to help with fluid balance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2170-06-03 11:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I remember last time I was bloated and short of breath when I missed one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2170-06-03 11:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Keeping your fluid status stable helps your heart and makes surgery safer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2170-06-03 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray is back. It shows mild cardiomegaly and a little fluid in the lungs, but no pneumonia or collapse. Your central line is in good position."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2170-06-03 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? The fluid in my lungs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2170-06-03 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s mild, and we expect it given your heart failure. Dialysis will help remove the extra fluid. We’ll monitor it closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2170-06-04 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your stress test was completed. Good news—no signs of cardiac ischemia. Cardiology cleared you for surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2170-06-04 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief! When will the surgery be?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2170-06-04 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Tomorrow morning. We’ll do dialysis today to optimize your volume status before the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2170-06-04 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. What about my blood sugars? They’ve been hard to control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2170-06-04 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your HbA1c was 8.2, which is elevated. We’ll manage your insulin carefully during your stay to keep sugars stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2170-06-04 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my antibiotics? I’ve been on vancomycin and ceftazidime at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2170-06-04 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve continued both for surgical prophylaxis. You’ll keep them with each dialysis session after surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2170-06-04 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You just finished dialysis. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2170-06-04 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. My legs feel less heavy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2170-06-04 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. That means the fluid removal is helping. Rest well tonight. Surgery is at 8 a.m. tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2170-06-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, Ms. ___. You made it through the surgery. You had a left below-the-knee amputation, and it went smoothly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2170-06-05 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. My leg… it’s gone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2170-06-05 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the lower part of your left leg was removed. The wound is closed with staples. We placed nerve catheters for pain control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2170-06-05 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I have a lot of pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2170-06-05 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re managing it well. The nerve catheters are helping. You’ll also get oral Dilaudid as needed. We’ll switch to a fentanyl patch soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2170-06-05 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The nerve catheters were removed this afternoon. How’s your pain now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2170-06-05 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still sore, but the pills help. The patch is on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2170-06-05 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the fentanyl patch is in place. It will help with ongoing limb pain. Your PCP will help wean it later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2170-06-06 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noticed a small amount of redness around your incision. It’s mild cellulitis, so we’re continuing vancomycin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2170-06-06 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? Could it get worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2170-06-06 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s mild and caught early. With antibiotics, it should resolve. We’ll keep a close eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2170-06-06 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t urinated much. I’ve had this problem before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2170-06-06 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your chart notes urinary retention. We catheterized you and got 350cc. We’ll monitor and avoid a Foley if possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2170-06-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Your incision is clean, and the redness is improving. Physical therapy saw you and recommends rehab."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2170-06-07 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Rehab? I’ll need help learning to move?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2170-06-07 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, to build strength, prevent knee contractures, and prepare for a prosthesis. You’ll go to an extended care facility."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2170-06-07 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. What about my blood thinners? I was on warfarin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2170-06-07 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Because of your history of HIT and calciphylaxis, we started apixaban instead. You’ll take it twice daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2170-06-07 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe after surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2170-06-07 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We held one dose when removing the nerve catheters. Now that healing is underway, it’s safe to continue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2170-06-08 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine culture came back with yeast. It’s likely related to your history of urogenital candidiasis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2170-06-08 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Do I need treatment?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2170-06-08 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. You’re not symptomatic, and it’s likely colonization. We’ll watch for symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2170-06-09 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your incision is healing well. The mild cellulitis is resolving. We’ll keep the antibiotics for two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2170-06-09 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the fentanyl patch? I’m worried about being on strong pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2170-06-09 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll wean it slowly after discharge. Your PCP will help manage that to avoid withdrawal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2170-06-10 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Cardiology updated your meds: atorvastatin 80 mg daily and lisinopril increased to 20 mg. Imdur and hydralazine are stopped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2170-06-10 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Why the change?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2170-06-10 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "To better protect your heart and kidneys. Atorvastatin lowers cholesterol, and higher-dose lisinopril helps your heart function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2170-06-11 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re making great progress. PT says you can transfer using your right foot. No weight on the left side yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2170-06-11 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How long before I can walk with a prosthesis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2170-06-11 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It takes weeks to months. First, the wound must fully heal. Then rehab will train you gradually."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2170-06-12 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning your discharge tomorrow. You’ll go to a rehab facility for continued care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2170-06-12 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What do I need to watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2170-06-12 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call if you have fever, increased redness, drainage, or new pain. Keep the site elevated and don’t soak it in water."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2170-06-12 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my diet?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2170-06-12 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue your diabetic, low-fat diet. Weigh yourself daily—call if you gain over 3 pounds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2170-06-13 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared for discharge. You’ll go to ___ rehab facility."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2170-06-13 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’m nervous but ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2170-06-13 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well. Continue vancomycin and ceftazidime with dialysis for two weeks. Follow up with vascular surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2170-06-13 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the apixaban?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2170-06-13 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, apixaban twice daily. No driving until your surgeon clears you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2170-06-13 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll follow all the instructions. Thank you for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2170-06-13 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Rehab will help you adjust. We’re here if you need anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2170-06-13 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing—should I stop smoking?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2170-06-13 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, strongly. Smoking narrows blood vessels and harms circulation, especially important now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2170-06-13 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try. My PCP can help?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2170-06-13 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they can provide support and resources. It’s one of the best things you can do for healing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2170-06-13 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need help at home after rehab?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2170-06-13 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re wheelchair-dependent now. Services will be arranged based on your progress in rehab."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2170-06-13 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my eye? I can’t see out of the right one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2170-06-13 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your retinopathy has caused blindness in that eye. Continue seeing your eye doctor regularly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2170-06-13 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just want to stay out of the hospital."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2170-06-13 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We all do. Managing your diabetes, heart, and wounds carefully will help keep you healthy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2170-06-13 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do my best."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2170-06-13 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s all we can ask. You’ve been through a lot, and you’re handling it well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2170-06-13 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2170-06-13 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Call your doctor if anything changes. Safe travels to rehab."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2170-06-13 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2170-06-13 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send a summary to your PCP so they can help manage your pain meds and follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2170-06-13 12:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I don’t want to be in pain or confused about my meds."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2170-06-03 11:30:00",
    "admission_end": "2170-06-13 15:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes, end-stage renal disease on dialysis, chronic heart failure, and atrial fibrillation was admitted for cardiac optimization prior to a left below-the-knee amputation due to a chronic non-healing calcaneal ulcer. She underwent preoperative cardiac clearance with a P-MIBI stress test showing no ischemia. She continued her regular hemodialysis schedule and was started on vancomycin and ceftazidime for surgical prophylaxis. The amputation was performed without complications, and nerve catheters were placed for pain control, later replaced by a fentanyl patch. Mild incisional cellulitis developed postoperatively, managed with continued antibiotics. Due to a history of HIT and calciphylaxis, she was transitioned from warfarin to apixaban. Physical therapy recommended inpatient rehabilitation, and she was discharged to an extended care facility with plans to continue antibiotics with dialysis, wound monitoring, and follow-up with vascular surgery.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with peripheral circulatory disorders, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage V or end stage renal disease",
      "Unspecified disorder of autonomic nervous system",
      "Chronic diastolic heart failure",
